\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Minima $a^{*}$ of $f(a)$ for different configurations of $R$ (of characteristic $q$ and degree $\deg (R)+1$), witness sizes $\ell $, and $\tau $ such that $\ell _1=\ell ^\tau $. By choosing primes in the interval $[2^{a^*}, 2^{114}]$, we have that the first error term $\kappa _0^*$ satisifes $\kappa _0^* = 1/2^{-\log f(a^*)}$. We include the bits left required to achieve $\kappa _0^* < 1/2^{128}$ and the cost of grinding such amount of bits, in a MacBook Air M4 16GB, multi-threaded, using Blake3 as hash function. We omit configurations whose grinding cost exceeds $\approx 150$ms; in particular $\tau =0.6$ is omitted for larger $\ell $.}}{35}{table.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
